    "body": "# Bounty: Clarify the unresolved BT9 real-host hook evidence in BACKLOG\n\nid bt-26bb9883d6b2 · created 2026-10-13T12:54:57.037Z by box-bounty@0.1.0\n\n## What is wanted\n\nClarify the unresolved BT9 real-host hook evidence\n\nIn BACKLOG.md, add a short factual note distinguishing BT9's tested hook adapters and file/command wiring from its unmet acceptance requirement that two actual agent hosts fire the hook. Read waves/BT9.md and preserve its stated evidence limits. Do not claim that installation or a manually invoked command proves an actual host fired a hook.\n\nChange only BACKLOG.md. Do not change any hook, setting, instruction file or test. This second zero-reward bounty is also the second open issue for BT10's public-format reader check and may close with no solution after that check.\n\n## What was already tried\n\nNo public note was supplied.\n\n## The code\n\nBranch from `box-bounty/bt-26bb9883d6b2` — it is the branch pull requests for this bounty target.\nThe branch is based on commit dc71f2ba28a3a988dc174b5aa47e44b27e70d9b3, the newest commit this repository already had: it points at that commit — nothing new was published.\n\n## How to answer\n\nFork this repository (or push a branch inside it), branch from `box-bounty/bt-26bb9883d6b2`, make the change, and open a pull request against `box-bounty/bt-26bb9883d6b2` in this repository. Collecting an answer runs nothing you wrote — the poster reads the change and decides.\n\nNobody is known to be watching these issues yet. Anyone can read this issue and the branch, and any account may answer.\n\nreward: $0\nThe merged solution earns the whole reward. Other solutions and parts used by hand earn nothing.\nlicence: LICENSE (package.json declares Apache-2.0)\n\n<!-- box-bounty:bt-26bb9883d6b2 -->\n<!-- box-bounty-format\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"kind\":\"box-bounty\",\"id\":\"bt-26bb9883d6b2\",\"repository\":\"shouteck/omakase-box\",\"workCommit\":\"dc71f2ba28a3a988dc174b5aa47e44b27e70d9b3\",\"branc